orizes typed alias): killed per the attached logs. Not re-run by me.\012\012## Findings\012\012```json\012[]\012```\012\012## Surface table (the brief supplied no table; rows are reviewer-derived, highest risk first, and carry rev-1'"'"'s row ids)\012\012| Row | Result | Attack / evidence |\012| --- | --- | --- |\012| R1 workload snapshot-bound selection | held | (a) rev-1 overlay repro, 5/5 pass. (b) New attack `TestReviewAttackSnapshotBoundAliasSuppressedAfterQuery` (overlay): alias-only `["sol","luna"]` ceiling, snapshot recommends `sol`. The canonical group `codex-unmapped:gpt-6-sol` is suppressed BEFORE the query: live admission degrades to gpt-6-luna and runSpawn refuses `workload_class_snapshot_stale ... resolved codex/gpt-6-luna/low instead of ... codex/sol/low`, with 0 launches. When it is suppressed AFTER the query, the digest is stale and the spawn is refused with 0 launches. Genuine drift through the real entry point is refused, which covers the developer'"'"'s surviving `drift-01` bound at class level. Log: `attack-suppression-01.log`. |\012| R2 limit selection alias/head collapse (AC1, AC2) | held | Re-ran the `TestSpawnAliasCeilingsRecordExecutedIdentityWithoutLimitDegradation` family in the focused cmd run. Code-read `CanonicalizeAdmittedPairs`: an effort union only covers efforts already admitted for the same executed model. The frozen `SelectionPolicySnapshot` stores the same canonical set (`cmd/spawn_limits.go:433`), so a limit-retry replay agrees with preflight, and `Verify()` recomputes the digest from those canonical pairs. |\012| R3 literal admission unchanged (AC3) | held | Re-ran `TestHeadOnlyCeilingStillRefusesAliasWithoutFallback` and `TestRunSpawnWorkloadSnapshotDoesNotAdmitUnlistedAliasByHeadEquivalence`. A grep for model equality on `Resolved.Model` / `SelectedModel` in non-test cmd/internal code finds only the fixed gate. |\012| R4 choosePair seed tie (AC4) | held | `internal/spawn` full package green (`TestChoosePairPrefersSurvivingSeedOnInjectedRankTie`). Both the max and min branches carry `order == 0 && model == seed.Model`. |\012| R5 genuine suppression still degrades (AC5) | held | `TestSuppressedCanonicalAliasGroupStillDegrades` green, plus R1(b) above. See note N-A on pre-fix alias-group state. |\012| R6 launch argv (AC6) | held | `TestRunSpawnAliasProductionConfigBuildsCanonicalLaunchArgv` captures `spawn.Config.Model` from runSpawn'"'"'s `spawnNewRun` and passes it to `spawn.BuildCommand` (rev-1 N2 closed). |\012| R7 `--ack-resolved` with aliased resolved pair | held | New attack `TestReviewAttackAckResolvedAlias` (overlay, `adjustment_confirmation: required`). An unadjusted alias launches without an ack. An ack on an unadjusted alias is refused with `selection_confirmation_not_allowed`. With an alias `resolution_model`, the ack `sol/low` is refused with `resolved_selection_ack_required` ("selection changed gpt-6-luna/low -> gpt-6-sol/low"). The ack `gpt-6-sol/low` passes the ack match and stops at the two-step `resolved_selection_rationale_required` history rule, which my single-invocation harness does not satisfy; that is expected protocol, not a defect. A missing ack is refused. N1 docs sentence is present in SKILL.md and references/tracked-background-spawn.md. Log: `attack-ack-01.log`. |\012| R8 restart / limit-retry successors | held | Code read plus the R2 evidence. A restart copies `manifest.Model` (the head) with no re-admission. A limit retry replays the canonical frozen snapshot with seed `cfg.Model` (the head), and `providerLimitGroupOf(cfg.Model)` now records hits under the head group. Queued preparation re-admits from `typedModel`. |\012\012Free hunt: I traced every production consumer of the canonical value (ack gate, limit-retry snapshot, group attribution on a limit hit, restart), which produced R7 and R8 above and note N-A. No blocking mechanism reproduced.\012\012## Notes (non-blocking)\012\012- N-A (transitional, cannot be classified by the AC): a suppression that a base binary recorded for an alias run is keyed on the alias group (`codex-unmapped:sol`, because base used `cfg.Model = sol`). The candidate no longer consults that group: overlay `TestReviewAttackAliasGroupSuppression` shows resolved=gpt-6-sol with no degradation (log `attack-alias-group-01.log`). The exposure is bounded by the suppression window. After the upgrade the first hit is recorded under the head group and handled by the retry plane. Base had the mirror-image gap (a head hit never suppressed the alias). Consider a follow-up that folds alias groups into their head group in the group table.\012- N-B: `TestWorkloadResolvedPairRejectsGenuineExecutedDrift` covers `sol` only, so a per-alias narrowing of the drift gate for another alias would survive it. R1(b) shows the class is refused end-to-end. This is not blocking.\012- #297: typed-head and typed-alias snapshot-bound Muse paths both admit and record `muse-spark-1.3-contributor` (the muse subtests of the committed workload test pass). The rev-1 mirrored failure is gone. Closing GitHub #297 itself stays out of scope, as the brief requires.\012- Base drift: origin/main has moved past `46811b1e` and touches overlapping files (per finalization-rev2f). The integrating run must rebase and revalidate.\012- Environment: the host disk hit 100% mid-review. I freed about 2 GB by pruning Go build-cache entries not accessed for 2+ days. No project files were touched.\012\012## Validation re-run by the reviewer (exact candidate)\012\012| Command | Exit | Log |\012| --- | ---: | --- |\012| `go test ./internal/spawn -count=1` | 0 | internal-spawn-01.log |\012| `go test ./cmd -run '"'"'TestSpawnAlias\|TestHeadOnlyCeiling\|TestSuppressedCanonicalAlias\|TestRunSpawnAlias\|TestRunSpawnWorkloadBoundAlias\|TestRunSpawnWorkloadSnapshotDoesNotAdmit\|TestWorkloadSnapshotRegistryRowsBindLiveAliasTargets\|TestWorkloadResolvedPairRejectsGenuineExecutedDrift\|TestRunSpawnRefusesLiveAdmissionPairDrift\|TestRunSpawnWorkloadGateRefuses\|Test