 ## 2026-09-24
 
-### TASK-260830-g0pcnt rework rev6 — physical path-depth bound
+### TASK-260830-g0pcnt rev6 revalidation — path-derived length forms
+
+- TRANSITIVE GUARD: Extended the test-only AST taint analysis to keep path provenance through `strings.Split`, range indices over path components, numeric length/count expressions, and `[]byte(path)` conversions. The generator still sweeps the physical Darwin limit; the extra guard now rejects structural caps expressed as split-component count, range index, or byte length as well as direct separator/depth comparisons.
+- MUTANTS: Added `N-ancestor-walk-split-component-count-cap`, `N-ancestor-walk-range-index-cap`, and `N-ancestor-walk-byte-length-cap`; each was run alone twice and each produced a raw Go test exit 1 with its named ancestor-walk test failing. `callee24` and `isFilesystemRoot` cap mutants were also rerun alone twice after the final guard edit and killed. An applied line-count-preserving `C-control` survived. The first range-index plant attempt failed to link with `no space left on device`; it was excluded, then two isolated retries killed it.
+- VALIDATION: All 45 packages passed the configured verbose test gate in ten current bounded groups, all 45 passed coverage in ten current groups, and all 17 configured fuzz runs passed. Race groups passed for all packages except `sessquery`, whose current ten-minute-bounded attempt was interrupted at 9:48 (real exit 1, no test failure output); the prior rev6 `sessquery` race result (409.416s, exit 0) is reused because this revalidation changed only tmuxserver tests and the Python mutant harness, not that package or its production dependencies. The current tmuxserver race and coverage groups both exited 0. Determinism rerun of custody tests at `-count=3`, build, native vet, Windows vet/build, tracecheck, catalog check, JSON parse, task-board validate, and diff check exited 0. A monolithic `go test ./... -count=1 -v` attempt was interrupted (real exit 1); the complete package set passed in the bounded groups instead.
+- EVIDENCE: Current-run logs and the exact package reuse rationale are in `.temp/TASK-260830-g0pcnt/rev6-current/`. Registry, README, importer grid, production code, and the 4-of-4 acceptance ratio did not change in this revalidation. No tmux process or real socket is required.
+
+### TASK-260830-g0pcnt rework rev6 — physical path-depth bound (initial validation)
 
 - PATH DOMAIN: The walk-length fixture now reaches `unix.PathMax-1` instead of stopping at a selected test depth. On Darwin the generated runtime-root path is 1023 bytes, with 452 one-byte nested directories and 460 ancestor positions. `TestCustodyAncestorWalkGeneratedDepthToPathMax` plants mode 0777 at the deepest and middle non-root ancestors and asserts the literal `tmux_unsafe_socket_path` refusal. The deep derived socket exceeds `sun_path`, so the physical-depth test drives the shared predicate directly.
 - ENTRY WIRING: `TestCustodyAncestorWalkReachableFromProductionEntries` mechanically confirms Probe, Spawn, and Execute reach `CheckSocketCustody` and the same `checkCustodyAncestors` predicate.
